# Shared kernel

## Purpose

The part of the model that at least two contexts use and own together: value objects, their
refusals, and the schemas several contexts answer with (`presentation/`). Every change needs the
agreement of each context that imports it. A file one context alone reads belongs to that
context.

## Ubiquitous language

The words of the shared kernel, which every context that imports it agrees on. A word with
another meaning in one context is that context's, in its own glossary.

